# Caddyfile for a server that hosts WellSim AND NOTHING ELSE.
#
# THE DOMAIN CHANGED, 11 September 2026. This file served `wellsim.app` until
# that name was retired on 8 September (its Cloudflare zone is empty and it no
# longer resolves, though the registration is still the owner's). WellSim
# relaunches on **wellssim.app** — note the DOUBLE S — bought from Spaceship
# on 11 September. The blocks below name the new domain. Everything else is
# verbatim from the old box, which is why the file is otherwise unchanged.
#
# Install as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on the new server. Caddy gets its own
# Let's Encrypt certificate the first time DNS points here and 80/443 are
# open; nothing needs copying from the old machine, which no longer holds any
# WellSim certificate or config.
#
# PORT 80 IS NOT OPTIONAL. Caddy needs it for the ACME HTTP challenge before
# it can serve 443 at all. And `.app` is on the HSTS preload list, so browsers
# force HTTPS for this name with no click-through: until the certificate
# issues, the site is unreachable rather than merely insecure.
#
# /var/log/caddy must exist and be writable by the caddy user, or the log
# directive fails at startup.
#
# THE www BLOCK NEEDS A www DNS RECORD. As of 11 Sep, www.wellssim.app does
# not resolve. Caddy will keep retrying ACME for a name that points nowhere
# and fill the log with failures. Either create the record alongside the apex
# one, or delete the www block below — do not leave it half-configured.

wellssim.app {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3355
    # access log added 1 Sep 2026 — the site had NO traffic record since launch
    log {
        output file /var/log/caddy/wellsim.access.log {
            roll_size 10MB
            roll_keep 10
        }
    }
}
www.wellssim.app {
    redir https://wellssim.app{uri} permanent
}
